What these files are
--------------------

One file per city, written by `npm run seo:data` (see
`apps/frontend/scripts/fetch-poi-data.mjs`), holding the results of Overpass
queries against OpenStreetMap: element ids, names, coordinates, and a handful
of tags — addresses, opening hours, wheelchair access, fees.

Two fields are derived rather than copied. `context` is the name of the
building or park a point stands inside, and `street` the name of the road it
stands beside, both worked out at fetch time from the geometry of other
OpenStreetMap objects. They are OpenStreetMap data too, and are covered here
along with everything else.


What that means if you use them
-------------------------------

Attribution. Any public use must credit "© OpenStreetMap contributors" and
link to https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright.

Share-Alike. If you publicly use an adapted version of this database, or
anything built from a substantial part of it that is itself a database, that
work must be offered under the ODbL as well.

A Produced Work — a map, a page, an image made by querying this data — needs
attribution but is not itself bound by Share-Alike. The prerendered pages this
repository builds are such a work, which is why they carry the credit rather
than this licence.
